  "question": {
    "text": "An electron of hydrogen atom on an excited state is having energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>. The maximum number of allowed transitions to lower energy level is _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit is given by, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>No of transition,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p>"
  }
}